A NOTE ON CREDIT (not a licence condition)

The copyright above covers this software. The *method* it implements does not
originate here and is credited separately.

The 30-day content calendar - the five post types (EDUCATE, PROOF, ENGAGE,
OFFER, MIRROR) and the five-day rotation they turn on - is
themarketingfmpodcast's work. The creator growth practices behind the profile
audit and the content-style analysis are @teezytheturtle's.

Every report, spreadsheet and document this tool produces carries the line:

    themarketingfmpodcast - Free Tool, Share it.

and the code checks for it before writing anything, so it is not dropped by
accident. That check is a courtesy the tool does to itself, not a restriction
on you: the licence above is plain MIT and the software is genuinely free to
use, modify and redistribute. If you fork this and want the tag gone, edit
tta/attribution.py and regenerate the digest - nothing here forbids it.

Keeping the credit is simply the decent thing to do, and it costs you a line.
